<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Han Lin'er</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1366</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Han Lin'er was the son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-lotus">White Lotus</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-shantong">Han Shantong</a>, who launched the Red Turban revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> in 1351. In 1355 rebel commanders proclaimed him emperor of a restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a> rose under his banner. He drowned in 1366 while being brought to Zhu, who founded the Ming two years later.</p></div>
